WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.071
♪♪

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.339
-Why sit behind a desk?

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.507
-Why sit behind a desk?
-Yeah, I never get that.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:09.976
-It's a power move.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.979
-This guy's horrible. Don't
listen to a word he has to say.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.280
-Delete and block.
Delete and block.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.349
-One sec.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.151
Hell, no!

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.053
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.521
-A top CDC official,

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:23.556
the director
of the national center

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.092
for immunization
and respiratory diseases,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.793
said this week
it was inevitable

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:30.129
and that disruption to
everyday life may be severe.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:31.965
So, you can either believe
that expert,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.567
a doctor and scientist who's
received numerous awards

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.302
and worked in public health
for decades,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.138
or you can believe this expert.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.207
-The virus --
They're working hard.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.109
Looks like by April,
you know, in theory,

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.178
when it gets a little warmer,
it miraculously goes away.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:47.881
Hope that's true.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.916
-What?

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.518
What are you talking about?

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:54.253
It will go away
when it gets warmer?

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:58.357
We're talking about a possible
pandemic, not winter skin.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:01.560
Cable news reacted with shock
at Bernie's success in Nevada.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.630
For example,
as results were coming in

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.465
and it was clear
that young voters

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.067
and people of color were going
overwhelmingly for Sanders,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.870
one anchor at a caucus site
audibly sighed

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.237
as she reported the results.

00:01:12.237 --> 00:01:14.640
-Largely people of color.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.476
Of those, the majority
are Latino,

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:21.581
and they are clearly,
at least from eyeballing it,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:25.318
[sighs] strongly in favor
of Bernie Sanders

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.553
with Joe Biden coming in second.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.056
-Oh, my God with the sigh!

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.659
She's reporting on Bernie
winning a caucus site

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.262
the way you tell your parents
why your dip[bleep] boyfriend

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.598
got fired from his job.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:43.602
Well, he was using the copier,
and, well, from eyeballing it,

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:46.172
it looks like he, uh -- [Sighs]

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.609
He photocopied his ass
and put it up in the break room.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.044
One thing
that I was very impressed with

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:56.282
is we drew song titles
that we did not see in advance

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.985
and then were told to give
five minutes to write a song.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.320
You guys wrote a very good song
in five minutes.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.389
It was disheartening.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.424
-It was really scandalous.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.294
I will say it's the most
beautiful song I've ever heard

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.030
that has a line about 69ing.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.798
-I think we're going to lean
into the comedy of the show.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:14.433
-Yeah, I think
it's about time, right?

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:15.502
Yeah, 'cause I will say --

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.203
and I don't want
to be critical of it --

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.837
very few laughs in the first
three seasons.

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:20.406
-Very few laughs.
And we've taken that note.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.608
We understand that,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.509
and we're going to lean into
the comedy of it.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:24.843
-I feel like that's
what we're missing, is, like,

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:27.313
we would love to see the blooper
reel from "Handmaid's."

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.649
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.419
-Just with a lot of terrible
sound effects like "Wah, wah."

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.888
-You said that my show gave you

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.057
a new way to think
about a part of your body.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.225
The penis specifically.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.227
-I think about my penis
differently, yeah.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.430
-You describe it as the --
It's the most feminine.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.031
-Yes, it's a feminine object.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:47.700
At very least,
it's all the stereotypes

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.203
that are applied to women are
something that you could apply

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.737
to the penis, you know?
The classic ones.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.973
The sort of,
"Oh, they're so sensitive.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.442
They're needy. They nag you.
They poke you in the night.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.844
Oh, are you awake?
I'm awake."

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:02.715
-Are you lonely?
Looking to meet someone new?

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:06.185
Then call the Charlie Brown
adults-only hot line now

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.387
to make a very special friend.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.489
-So, uh...what are you wearing?

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:14.193
-Wa wa wawa wa wawa.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.295
-Good grief.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:20.233
-You had you a job at
a very highly revered website.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.534
-It was revered.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.569
-Was it revered at the time?
I don't remember well.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.871
But it was Suck.com.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:30.042
-Yeah. And when you say it like
that, you make it sound dirty.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.311
The website's gone, by the way.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.079
It's vanished.
You can't get it anymore.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.613
But it was "suck" for, like,
"This sucks,"

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:38.851
not for whatever you thought.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.086
-What do you think I thought
it was?!

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:45.524
-I don't know but it seemed
like you were judging!

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:48.394
I love talking to people,
especially from my era,

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.096
and their failed sketches.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.530
You had one with Snoop.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.233
-It's 20 years later,
I see Snoop, and he's like,

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:58.471
"Finesse, why they didn't do
'The A-pimp-tice'?"

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.506
Donald Trump had come
on the show the week before

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.641
we did this
big "Apprentice" sketch.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:04.276
So, Snoop comes on
the week after,

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:08.381
and he ads has this grand idea
to do "The A-pimp-tice."

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.916
And instead of saying
"You're fired,"

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.719
I'll just smack a chick
and say, "You tired."

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.689
And I was like, "Yeah, Snoop,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.659
I don't think NBC gonna let you
smack anybody."

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.228
-What was it like
working with them?

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.864
-Oh, it's unbelievable because
my daughter was 8 at the time,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.765
and it was in the day
in the last century

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:27.967
when it was answering machines,

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.568
before mobile phones
and the Internet.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.371
It was a little,
red bleeping sign,

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.205
and she pressed the button
when she came home from school,

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:36.309
and it said, "We offered you
the Spice World manager

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.810
in "Spice World," the movie,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.244
and she went
absolutely ballistic.

00:04:39.244 --> 00:04:40.480
And she said,
"Dad, you've got to do it!

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.813
Dad, you've got to do it!"
So, I did,

00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:45.784
and I had playground status
for the next two terms.

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:48.054
[ Laughter ]
I was a god.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.290
-I just want to take a moment to
just celebrate the simple fact

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.925
of being on television.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:57.263
♪♪

